id: pm-jev-sdk-host-alignment
title: Adopt pm-cli 2026.11.24 host-aligned SDK behaviour
description: Migrate the pinned PM toolchain and align registered policy commands with the native host on plain trackers. Companion item pm-cli-website-spus.
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-24T15:22:01.303Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T19:41:14.530Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Pin the current first-party SDK toolchain with refreshed lockfiles.; Prove registered policy commands and typed refusals on plain trackers and preserve published dependency bullets.; Pass package release gates and verify the committed build.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T18:52:21.185Z","harness:claude-code","Finished by the orchestrator after the agent's provider login was revoked mid-run. On pm-cli 2026.11.24 the host evaluates beforeMutation guards during preview as well as commit and passes actor and dry_run. dedupe.ts adapts the close guard: a preview (dry_run) neither records nor consumes a pending closure, and a pending closure is bound to the author that requested it, so another actor cannot consume it; receipt, revision and deadline are still checked on commit. Tests in dedupe, cost-policy, counterfactual and replay-command follow the declared options and the new guard context. All four changelog entry points pass --dependency-updates. Orchestrator gates on the committed tree: build, typecheck, lint, changelog:check, 59/59 in the four touched test files, the changelog-flag and release-workflow tests. The full npm and Bun release gates were not run locally: CI certifies them on the PR."
  "2026-11-24T19:41:14.530Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (CodeRabbit on dedupe.ts): a closing receipt from another author could replace a live pending closure, after which the owner's close failed its author check and the other author could close with their own receipt. The guard now refuses a different author's closing receipt while a pending closure for the item is live (jev_stale_inference, the same in preview and commit); the owning author may record again, and an expired pending closure no longer blocks anyone. New test 'a pending closure cannot be replaced by another author's receipt until it expires' fails when the check is removed (revert proof run). The existing peer test now asserts that the peer's preview is refused too, instead of allowed: a preview that allows a write the commit refuses would be wrong. Build, typecheck, lint, 60/60 in the four touched test files."
